  "cards": [
    {
      "id": "c_title",
      "accent": { "position": "right", "assetId": "img_leaf" },
      "notes": "Open by asking what a plant eats. Pause after the quote.",
      "body": [
        {
          "id": "b_title",
          "type": "heading",
          "level": 1,
          "text": "Introduction to Photosynthesis"
        },
        {
          "id": "b_lead",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Plants turn **sunlight**, water, and air into {color:primary}chemical energy{/color}."
        },
        {
          "id": "b_quote",
          "type": "quote",
          "text": "A leaf is a quiet factory that runs on light.",
          "cite": "Classroom notes"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "c_process",
      "background": { "kind": "gradient", "from": "#e7f5ea", "to": "#fff6d8", "angle": 135 },
      "notes": "Walk the two columns from left to right.",
      "body": [
        { "id": "b_process_heading", "type": "heading", "level": 2, "text": "The short version" },
        {
          "id": "n_process_stack",
          "type": "stack",
          "gap": "md",
          "children": [
            {
              "id": "n_process_columns",
              "type": "columns",
              "widths": [1.2, 1],
              "gap": "md",
              "align": "start",
              "children": [
                [
                  {
                    "id": "b_overview",
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "Carbon dioxide and water, plus light, become glucose and oxygen."
                  },
                  {
                    "id": "b_steps",
                    "type": "list",
                    "style": "number",
                    "items": [
                      "Capture light",
                      {
                        "text": "Split water",
                        "children": ["Release oxygen", "Keep the electrons"]
                      },
                      "Build sugar"
                    ]
                  }
                ],
                [
                  {
                    "id": "b_leaf",
                    "type": "image",
                    "assetId": "img_leaf",
                    "fit": "cover",
                    "width": "full",
                    "caption": "See a [diagram of a leaf](https://example.com/leaf)."
                  }
                ]
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "c_inside",
      "body": [
        { "id": "b_where", "type": "heading", "level": 3, "text": "Where it happens" },
        {
          "id": "b_chlorophyll",
          "type": "callout",
          "tone": "info",
          "text": "Chlorophyll lives in **chloroplasts**, mostly in the *mesophyll* of the leaf.\n\nThat green pigment is what makes the leaf look {highlight:yellow}green{/highlight}."
        },
        {
          "id": "n_organelles",
          "type": "grid",
          "columns": 2,
          "gap": "sm",
          "children": [
            {
              "id": "b_light_reactions",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Light reactions sit in the thylakoid membrane."
            },
            {
              "id": "b_checklist",
              "type": "list",
              "style": "check",
              "items": [
                { "text": "Thylakoids", "checked": true },
                { "text": "Stroma", "checked": false }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b_stages",
          "type": "table",
          "header": true,
          "rows": [
            ["Stage", "Location", "Output"],
            ["Light reactions", "Thylakoid", "ATP and oxygen"],
            ["Calvin cycle", "Stroma", "Sugar"]
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b_equation",
          "type": "code",
          "language": "text",
          "code": "6 CO2 + 6 H2O + light -> C6H12O6 + 6 O2"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "c_review",
      "body": [
        {
          "id": "b_review_heading",
          "type": "heading",
          "level": 2,
          "text": "Check your understanding"
        },
        {
          "id": "b_question",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "align": "center",
          "text": "Why do leaves look {color:green}green{/color} if they use other colors of light?"
        },
        {
          "id": "b_answers",
          "type": "list",
          "style": "bullet",
          "items": ["Green light is reflected", "Other colors are absorbed"]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "c_inputs",
      "accent": { "position": "left", "assetId": "img_sun" },
      "body": [
        {
          "id": "b_inputs_heading",
          "type": "heading",
          "level": 2,
          "text": "What the leaf collects"
        },
        {
          "id": "b_inputs_copy",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Think of light as the fuel, and `CO2` as the carbon source. The leaf does not *eat* soil."
        },
        {
          "id": "b_inputs_note",
          "type": "callout",
          "tone": "success",
          "text": "If students remember only one sentence, let it be this: light reactions charge the battery, and the Calvin cycle spends it."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "c_water",
      "accent": { "position": "top", "assetId": "img_drop" },
      "body": [
        { "id": "b_water_heading", "type": "heading", "level": 2, "text": "Water's path" },
        {
          "id": "b_water_copy",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Water enters through the roots, climbs the xylem, and reaches the mesophyll. A little is split. Most of it leaves again as vapor."
        },
        {
          "id": "b_water_list",
          "type": "list",
          "style": "bullet",
          "items": ["Roots take up water", "Xylem carries it upward", "Stomata let vapor out"]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "c_equation",
      "accent": { "position": "background", "assetId": "img_formula" },
      "body": [
        {
          "id": "b_equation_heading",
          "type": "heading",
          "level": 2,
          "text": "The equation, up close"
        },
        {
          "id": "b_equation_copy",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Count the atoms before you leave the slide. Six carbons in, one glucose out. A readable walk-through lives in the [class handout](https://example.com/equation)."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "c_palette",
      "background": { "kind": "color", "value": "#f3f7f4" },
      "body": [
        {
          "id": "b_palette_heading",
          "type": "heading",
          "level": 2,
          "text": "Look inside one cell"
        },
        {
          "id": "b_cell",
          "type": "image",
          "assetId": "img_cell",
          "fit": "contain",
          "width": "full",
          "caption": "A chloroplast, drawn as a few stacked membranes."
        },
        {
          "id": "b_palette_copy",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Name the parts out loud: {color:accent}thylakoid{/color}, stroma, and the sugar that leaves for the rest of the plant."
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
